fujairah.tx:
👇 If Iran has indeed for the first time struck tankers during the actual ship-to-ship (STS) oil transfer process, that would mark a significant escalation. These transfers can take 24–48 hours, leaving vessels stationary and more vulnerable, often near Fujairah in the UAE or Sohar in Oman.

Notably, Iranian analysts have regularly highlighted such additional vulnerabilities in the parallel oil export routes that bypass the Strait of Hormuz or Iran’s designated transit corridor through it, which Tehran has yet to target, including:

-directly targeting STS transfers as they occur, rather than just the shuttles/tankers heading to VLCCs; 

-striking more critical pumping stations along Saudi Arabia’s East-West Pipeline; 

-or targeting the ports and surrounding infrastructure from which these shuttles/tankers depart.
